{"step_index":721,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T03:54:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-04T21:54:26-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-04T21:54:27-06:00\nShowing lines 1-81 of 81\n1: # Informe Forense en Vivo: Entrada a Fastboot, Diagnóstico de `watchdog_reboot` (`U-Boot 2015.01-g220e992`) y Solución Anti-Watchdog\n2: \n3: **Fecha de Captura:** 29 de Octubre de 2026  \n4: **Dispositivo Analizado:** `ZTE ZXV10 B866V2` (`SN: Z41220090388172`, `MAC: C4:74:1E:F6:BE:19`, `ProductID: 48100499007041200000C4741EF6BE19`)  \n5: **SoC / Bootloader:** `Amlogic G12A (S905X2) Rev E (28:E - 40:2)` — `U-Boot 2015.01-g220e992 (Sep 05 2023 - 04:13:01)`  \n6: **Interfaz UART:** `Silicon Labs CP210x USB to UART Bridge (COM8 @ 115200 bps)`  \n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## 1. Cronología Exacta de los 5 Reinicios Capturados en Vivo (`boot times 0` a `boot times 4`)\n11: \n12: Mediante el monitor de memoria en tiempo real ([`monitor_smartty.ps1`](./monitor_smartty.ps1)) sobre `SmarTTY.exe` (`PID 3284`), se reconstruyó la secuencia completa sin desconectar el puerto serie:\n13: \n14: | Ciclo (`BL2`) | Razón de Reinicio (`BL31` / `U-Boot`) | Qué Ocurrió Exactamente en Hardware y Firmware | Resultado |\n15: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n16: | **`boot times 0`** | `reboot_mode=cold_boot` | Encendido en frío con el botón de Reset presionado (`GPIOAO_3 == 0`). El kernel detecta `gpio_keypad_down_cnt: 60` y ejecuta `Restarting system with command 'recovery'`. | Entra a modo **Recovery** |\n17: | **`boot times 1`** | `bl31 reboot reason: 0xd` / `0x2` (`reboot_mode:::: update`) | U-Boot lee `[commannd:boot-recovery]` en la partición `misc`, desactiva Dolby (`recovery mode, need disable dolby`) y levanta la consola root `#` en UART. | Consola root `#` activa en Recovery |\n18: | **`boot times 2`** | `bl31 reboot reason: 0x7` (`reboot_mode:::: fastboot`) | Desde la consola root `#` se ejecutó `reboot bootloader`. U-Boot registra el gadget USB Fastboot (`g_dnl_register: g_dnl_driver.name = usb_dnl_fastboot`). Se lanza el script `.bat`: `cb_oem_cmd()` falla en `f_fastboot.c:1649` y acto seguido ejecuta `cmd cb_reboot is reboot-bootl\n<truncated 3421 bytes>\npira y reinicia la placa (`reboot_mode=watchdog_reboot`).\n64: * Ese reinicio de hardware **borra el registro volátil `bl31 reboot reason: 0x7`** (`fastboot`).\n65: * En el siguiente arranque, U-Boot ve `reboot_mode=watchdog_reboot`, comprueba la partición `misc` con `bcb uboot-command` (que ignora `bootonce-bootloader`), intenta leer `boot-recovery` de `misc` (`read boot-recovery from misc failed.`) y termina forzando **`ztebsp: bootcmd=bootsys`** (sistema Android normal).\n66: \n67: ---\n68: \n69: ## 3. Solución Implementada en 3 Capas (Aciertos y Mejoras)\n70: \n71: 1. **Capa 1 — Ancla Persistente en `/dev/block/misc` desde Recovery (`#`) antes de ir a Fastboot:**\n72:    Ejecutar en `SmarTTY` (consola root `#` de Recovery):\n73:    ```sh\n74:    echo -n \"boot-recovery\" > /dev/block/misc ; sync ; reboot bootloader\n75:    ```\n76:    * **Efecto:** El registro de hardware `BL31` (`0x7`) mete la placa inmediatamente a **Fastboot**. Pero si el Watchdog llega a disparar `watchdog_reboot`, U-Boot encuentra `boot-recovery` en `misc`, **bloquea `ztebsp: bootcmd=bootsys`** y regresa siempre a la consola root `#` de **Recovery**.\n77: 2. **Capa 2 — Enganche Inmediato `< 200 ms` sin `timeout` en [`FLASHEAR_B866V2_ANDROID12_SEGURO_SIN_PERDER_WIDEVINE.bat`](../11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE/FLASHEAR_B866V2_ANDROID12_SEGURO_SIN_PERDER_WIDEVINE.bat):**\n78:    * Se eliminó la pausa interactiva posterior y todos los `timeout /t 2` / `timeout /t 4`.\n79:    * El script valida primero el firmware y entra en un bucle rápido `:WAIT_FASTBOOT` que detecta la enumeración USB de `usb_dnl_fastboot` al instante, enviando `fastboot getvar version` y `fastboot oem \"watchdog off\"`.\n80: 3. **Capa 3 — Retenedor Keep-Alive Indefinido ([`RETENER_FASTBOOT_ANTI_WATCHDOG.bat`](./RETENER_FASTBOOT_ANTI_WATCHDOG.bat)):**\n81:    * Envía pulsos `fastboot getvar version` cada 2 segundos y `fastboot oem \"watchdog off\"` para mantener activa la máquina de estados USB de `f_fastboot.c` todo el tiempo que se requiera sin que el Watchdog reinicie la placa.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":722,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T03:54:27Z","input_tokens":2890,"cache_read_tokens":36737,"output_tokens":1142,"thinking":"The forensic report details issues related to fastboot and watchdog processes. The document suggests investigating the session logs for fastboot and watchdog to pinpoint the root cause of the observed behavior. It points to a need for detailed monitoring during fastboot sessions and how the watchdog interacts with these processes.\n\n\nThe watchdog timer within the U-Boot environment is likely the root cause. When the device is in U-Boot Fastboot mode and there's no continuous USB activity, the watchdog triggers a reboot after approximately 10-15 seconds. This reboot sequence then leads to the normal Android boot process. The \"bootonce-bootloader\" command isn't being executed, leading to the device booting normally instead.\n\n\nThe `B866V2-FlashATV12 - Evoca.bat` script's keep-alive loop, using `fastboot getvar version`, prevents the watchdog from rebooting the device during the flashing process. The `PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe` application's blocking console read at the end of the flashing sequence disables the keep-alive, triggering the watchdog and resulting in a normal Android boot. The key difference lies in the active keep-alive of `Evoca.bat` versus the blocking nature of the application.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"manage_task","args":{"Action":"\"status\"","TaskId":"\"5ecd42aa-1b9a-4dda-aec7-a32c9730884f/task-697\""}},{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter \\\"Name='cmd.exe' OR Name='fastboot.exe' OR Name='adb.exe' OR Name='PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe'\\\" | Select-Object ProcessId, Name, CommandLine\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Check running processes for Evoca.bat and ProgramaPerfecto.exe\""}}]}
